## run A (2026-06-10)
# bootstrap Verify wall-clock cost (AC-14; TC-07g) — real period-1600 fixtures; one-time deployer-side genesis verification
# Go wall-clock, machine-dependent — NOT comparable to on-chain CPU steps, NOT proving time
# go1.23.6 linux/amd64, 12 CPUs (full machine line: benchmarks/phase-2-circuit/bootstrap-verify-cost.md)
# N=100 samples/line (10 warm-ups discarded), runtime.GC() before each; MEDIAN is the headline (min/p95 shown — min is unstable across runs on this machine: turbo/thermal shifts the baseline); golden-datum assert EVERY end-to-end run
# decompression timed ONCE as the shared prelude (Verify's actual structure); (d)/(e) exclude it — the lines sum to ~ the end-to-end total; gap reported

end-to-end Verify                  min=146.32ms  median=161.85ms  p95=186.27ms   golden 100/100 (+10 warm-ups)

decompress prelude (serves d+e)    min=107.35ms  median=116.79ms  p95=142.15ms
(a) current@gindex-86 + checkpoint min=626µs  median=669µs  p95=850µs
(b) next@gindex-87                 min=616µs  median=666µs  p95=895µs
(c) finality@gindex-169            min=9µs  median=9µs  p95=15µs   (K=1000-batched)
(d) BLS sync-aggregate             min=2.61ms  median=2.72ms  p95=3.07ms
(e) two Poseidon commitments       min=35.03ms  median=36.59ms  p95=49.96ms

sum of line medians = 157.45ms vs end-to-end median = 161.85ms -> gap 4.4ms (+2.7%)   [the no-double-count cross-check]
sum of line minima  = 146.24ms vs end-to-end min    = 146.32ms -> gap 79µs (+0.1%)   [minima: per-loop machine states differ — not additive, shown for transparency]

